    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Made by Tesla for Tesla vehicles",
      "Swappable NEMA adapters set the current automatically",
      "Covers Level 1 and Level 2 with the right adapter",
      "Compact enough to live in the trunk",
      "Adapter system is the best travel setup here"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "NACS connector only; built for Teslas",
      "Some adapters are sold separately",
      "32A maximum, below a 40A wall unit"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The best travel charger for a Tesla, and a capable home charger on a 14-50.",
    "description": "Tesla's Mobile Connector is the reference design for a portable EV charger. It is a control box and cable with a NACS connector on one end and an interchangeable adapter on the other, and each adapter tells the unit what it is plugged into so it limits current automatically. On a household 15-amp outlet it charges slowly at Level 1; with the NEMA 14-50 adapter Tesla rates it at up to 32 amps, which is a full overnight refill for most daily driving. Tesla sells additional adapters for other common receptacles, including 30-amp dryer outlets, which makes it unusually flexible for travel and for visiting friends and family. Check which adapters come in the box you buy, because the bundle has changed over the years. It is designed for Tesla vehicles, so owners of other NACS-port cars should check their automaker's guidance first. For a Tesla driver who wants one charger for home and the road, this is the one."
  },
