      "Must not be used with extension cords"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A straightforward portable Level 2 cord for J1772 cars and any 14-50.",
    "description": "Lectron is one of the better-known names in EV charging accessories, and its 32-amp portable Level 2 charger is a simple, sensible product. Lectron lists it as a 240-volt, 32-amp charger with a NEMA 14-50 plug and a J1772 connector, which suits most non-Tesla EVs with a J1772 port and many cars that ship with a J1772 adapter. At 32 amps, it draws roughly 7.7 kilowatts, which is enough for an overnight refill of most daily driving, and it stays within the continuous-load limit on a 14-50 whether the breaker behind it is 40 or 50 amps. Because it is a portable cord rather than a wall unit, it can go in the trunk for trips to a relative's house or an RV park where EV charging is permitted. There are no scheduling or app features, so off-peak charging depends on your car's own timer. Lectron has also offered NACS versions of its chargers; choose the connector that matches your car."
  },
  {
