          <p>
            The max current column only matters if your circuit can supply it. A 32-amp portable on a 50-amp circuit and a 40-amp wall unit on the same circuit are both legal; a 40-amp unit on a 40-amp circuit is not. The section on the 80 percent rule below covers how that works.
          </p>

          <p>
            Connector type is the other column to read carefully. Most non-Tesla EVs sold before the industry's switch to the NACS port use J1772 for AC charging, and newer cars from several makers are moving to NACS. Adapters exist in both directions, but buying a charger that matches your car's port natively is the simplest choice.
